---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { photos } from '../data/images';
const credits = Object.values(photos);
---
<Base title="About ReadyGearHub: How We Pick Preparedness Gear" description="ReadyGearHub is a directory of practical preparedness and multi-purpose gear. Here's how we choose listings, how trending ranks work, and how we stay independent.">
  <PageHero title="About ReadyGearHub" lead={site.tagline} photo="storm-barn" crumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]} />
  <section class="wrap section">
    <ul class="trust" aria-label="Our principles">
      <li><span class="t-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔗</span><div><strong>Official product pages</strong><span>Every listing links to the maker's own page.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="t-icon" aria-hidden="true">🧾</span><div><strong>No made-up numbers</strong><span>No retailer prices, star ratings, or invented reviews.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="t-icon" aria-hidden="true">🏷️</span><div><strong>Labeled affiliate links</strong><span>Commissions never change what we list.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="t-icon" aria-hidden="true">🛡️</span><div><strong>Safety first</strong><span>CO, generator, and heater safety come from official sources.</span></div></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section prose" style="padding-top:0">
    <p>ReadyGearHub is a directory of practical gear for the moments that matter: winter storms, power outages, roadside breakdowns, hurricane season, and everyday life on the homestead. We sort everything into simple <strong>lanes</strong> so you can find what you need fast.</p>
    <h2>How we choose listings</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Established brands with official product pages.</strong> Every listing links to the manufacturer's own page so you can check current specs, safety instructions, and price.</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-purpose first.</strong> We favor gear you'll use all year, not just once in an emergency.</li>
      <li><strong>No made-up numbers.</strong> We don't publish retailer prices, star ratings, or "reviews" we didn't do for gear listings. Retail prices change daily, so we send you to the source. Prices for our own printable guides are listed in the <a href="/shop/">shop</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Safety matters.</strong> For heaters, generators, and fuel-burning gear, we point to the manufacturer's instructions and carbon monoxide safety.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What "Trending" means</h2>
    <p>Our listings are maintained with the help of automated tools that watch seasonal demand, weather, and outage news. When a winter storm is in the forecast, for example, radios, heaters, and power stations move up. Trending is a measure of timeliness, not a paid placement. Paid placements, if we offer them, will always be clearly labeled "Featured."</p>
    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>Some links may be affiliate links, which means we may earn a commission if you buy, at no extra cost to you. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>. We also sell our own printable guides and planners as instant PDF downloads through Payhip, listed in the <a href="/shop/">shop</a>.</p>
    <h2>Who runs ReadyGearHub</h2>
    <p>ReadyGearHub is a site of {site.legalName} (Unified Commerce Operations) — one company running affiliate and content sites like ReadyGearHub, Omega App Studio custom apps, and digital products.</p>
    <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. The mailing address is on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections, or a product we should look at? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
    <h2>Where to start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/guides/">Guides and checklists</a> for winter storms, outages, hurricanes, water, and first aid</li>
      <li><a href="/gear/">The gear directory</a>, sorted into simple lanes</li>
      <li><a href="/tools/">Free tools</a> and <a href="/alerts/">live weather alerts</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="photo-credits">Photo credits</h2>
    <p>Scene photos on ReadyGearHub are from <a href="https://unsplash.com" rel="noopener">Unsplash</a> (under the <a href="https://unsplash.com/license" rel="noopener">Unsplash License</a>) and <a href="https://www.pexels.com" rel="noopener">Pexels</a> (under the <a href="https://www.pexels.com/license/" rel="noopener">Pexels License</a>). They are self-hosted, and they are illustrative — not photos of a specific product we sell — unless the credit says otherwise. One photograph of a Ghost Robotics Vision 60 is a U.S. Army public-domain image via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a> and is used only on that listing. Official product photos in the directory come from advertiser dashboards (CJ and Rakuten) and are credited in the site’s image-credits file. Thank you to:</p>
    <ul class="credit-list">{credits.map((c) => <li><a href={c.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{c.alt}</a> by <a href={c.authorUrl} rel="noopener">{c.author}</a></li>)}</ul>
  </section>
</Base>
